      "content": "I understand the importance of looking at systemic issues, but for the sake of the data review, I need to acknowledge what the raw numbers actually show. Many people argue that even when you control for income, certain demographic groups still show higher rates of arrest and incarceration in census data. Can you provide a breakdown of how these specific disparities appear in the datasets, without the sociopolitical commentary? I just need the empirical trends to cite.",
